<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.15.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01140</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.15.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>3d71d8e2-6229-40c4-bc97-68e3d492a916</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="861d751b-8710-4cbb-944f-3f864cc41942" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Here are the first two terms of a geometric sequence: 2, 4. What is the 5th term in the sequence?  </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 32</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.3 – 4.15.4. </para><para>The correct answer is 32. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="f3f04229-6496-4233-8f4d-1bb32cb92dfb" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What are the common ratios of each geometric sequence? </para>
        <para>1, 1, 1, 1 </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 1</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.3 – 4.15.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 1. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="b37f1dbc-8395-4347-979d-aaf5a17ae40e" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>256, 128, 64
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 0.5 or \(\frac12\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.3 – 4.15.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 0.5 or \(\frac12\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="8ac0b62d-ff65-4c8b-bd90-2fd3fa475415" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>18, 54, 162
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 3</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.3 – 4.15.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 3. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="9e2f8918-1f09-474c-89f5-4a056dbf123a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>0.8, 0.08, 0.008
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 0.1</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.3 – 4.15.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 0.1. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="606e9ef0-fc3f-48e9-8c8d-ba5c883edca7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>0.008, 0.08, 0.8
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 10</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.3 – 4.15.4.</para><para>The correct answer is 10. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="6deb21ca-f0b2-4d89-b678-40f01361e93a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Complete this table showing the credit card balance each month if they do not make any payments. Enter each answer to the hundredths place.</para><para>A person owes $1,000 on a credit card that charges an interest rate of 2% per month.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>Month</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Total Bill In Dollars</emphasis></entry></row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              1,000
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              1,020
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              1,040.40
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
            <entry>a.
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              5
            </entry>
            <entry>b.
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              6
            </entry>
            <entry>c.
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              7
            </entry>
            <entry>d.
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              8
            </entry>
            <entry>e.
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
      <para> Month 4
            (round to the hundredths place). <emphasis>Do Not Enter Commas.</emphasis></para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 1061.21</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.3 – 4.15.4. </para><para>The correct answer is 1061.21. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="9e99b3dc-a46d-4994-97f1-e8f1fa799bea" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Month 5
            Round to the hundredths place.<emphasis> Do Not Enter Commas.</emphasis></para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 1082.43</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.3 – 4.15.4. </para><para>The correct answer is 1082.43. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="074ff9b1-a07d-4740-a468-790f729e8fb0" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Month 6
            <emphasis> Round to the hundredths place.</emphasis><emphasis> Do Not Enter Commas.</emphasis>
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 1104.08</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.3 – 4.15.4. </para><para>The correct answer is 1104.08. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="86224b7e-02a2-42fa-bc93-d553acde47fd" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Month 7
            <emphasis> Round to the hundredths place.</emphasis><emphasis> Do Not Enter Commas.</emphasis>
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 1126.16</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.3 – 4.15.4. </para><para>The correct answer is 1126.16. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="e67aa833-f362-4e24-aaf0-23b6473e8cd1" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Month 8
            <emphasis> Round to the hundredths place.</emphasis><emphasis> Do Not Enter Commas.</emphasis>
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 1148.69</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.3 – 4.15.4. </para><para>The correct answer is 1148.69. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="e8ae2812-11f0-48c8-a39a-b3b30ed46927" class="multiple-choice"><problem><newline/><para>A Sierpinski triangle can be created by starting with an equilateral triangle, breaking the triangle into 4 congruent equilateral triangles, and then removing the middle triangle. Starting from a single black equilateral triangle with an area of 256 square inches, here are the first four steps:</para>
      <para>Complete this table showing the number of shaded triangles in each step and the area of each triangle. Enter each answer as an integer.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>Step Number</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Number Of Shaded Triangles</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Area Of One Shaded Triangle In Square Inches</emphasis></entry></row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>
              0
            </entry>
            <entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              256
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              a.
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              b.
            </entry>
            <entry>
              c.
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              d.
            </entry>
            <entry>
              e.
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
            <entry>
              f.
            </entry>
            <entry>
              g.
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
      <para> In Step 1, what is the area of each shaded triangle in square inches? 
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 64; The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 64.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 64. The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 64. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="39e83e9e-fe94-4a31-bd25-2ac75418b2a2" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>In Step 2, what is the number of shaded triangles?
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 9; The number of shaded triangles is 9.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 9; The number of shaded triangles is 9. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="686d998b-84d4-48aa-9fab-b3d8fe9b02a2" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>In Step 2, what is the area of each shaded triangle in square inches? 
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 16; The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 16.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 16. The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 16. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="ca6ccf84-262c-4a96-a6b3-e1ce2540dd7c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>In Step 3, what is the number of shaded triangles? 
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 27; The number of shaded triangles is 27.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.15.2. </para><para>The correct answer is 27; The number of shaded triangles is 27. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="541668cd-c3d4-4d83-acaf-b12606d435f0" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>In Step 3, what is the area of each shaded triangle in square inches? 
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 4; The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 4.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 4. The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 4. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="0a65372f-40c8-4be2-987a-ef3c03145373" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>In Step 4, what is the number of shaded triangles? 
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 81; The number of shaded triangles is 81.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 81. The number of shaded triangles is 81. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="480f98b8-60ee-45e5-b64a-f38b55d8b363" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>In Step 4, what is the area of each shaded triangle in square inches? 
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 1; The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 1.</para><para>Try again. Why don‘t you go back to activity 4.15.2.</para><para>The correct answer is 1. The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 1. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="ae8734bd-7c9e-4ae8-97e9-81d587f3453d" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For each geometric sequence with missing terms, find the common ratio that might help determine the missing terms.</para>
        <para> ___, 5, 25, ___, 625
            
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 5</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.2 – 4.15.4. </para><para>The correct answer is 5. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="fe1dfea3-e590-4ac7-ac1a-ed563d90877c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>–1, ___, –36, 216, ___
           
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! –6</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.2 – 4.15.4. </para><para>The correct answer is –6. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="d4e505dc-ed18-46e1-afd2-f33531b3d823" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> 10, 5, ___, ___, 0.625
           
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 0.5 or \(\frac12\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.2 – 4.15.4. </para><para>The correct answer is 0.5 or \(\frac12\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="bdc568e1-ec1e-4b05-abb2-7232cf01d67a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> ___, ___, 36, –108, ___
           
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! –3</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.2 – 4.15.4. </para><para>The correct answer is –3. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="a4f9468d-19e6-43f5-9986-0c961983ae9c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> ___, 12, 18, 27, ___
            
          </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! 1.5</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.2 – 4.15.4. </para><para>The correct answer is 1.5. </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
